# Luminary marker — feat/488-a-real-trust-verb
- date: 2026-11-08
- lead: saltzer-schroeder — fail-safe defaults. A re-arm that depends on the
  publish path completing fails open. The marker carries its own deadline so
  the window closes whether the publish finished, failed or was cancelled.
- supporting:
  - john-ousterhout — the restore write now exists once. `do_on` and `rearm`
    both call it, so the two cannot drift apart.
  - linus-torvalds — `off`, `on` and `status` behave exactly as before. The
    two new verbs are additive.
